Provenance

The 0BSD above covers this repository as an AUR submission: the Maintainer
line, the $CARCH source token, the written rationale for version-pinning the
asset instead of resolving "latest", the release-bump changes this
repository's git history records, and this document.

It does not cover the base wording of PKGBUILD and cordial-bin.install,
which comes from the Cordial project's packaging/aur/cordial-bin/ directory
at https://github.com/luohoa97/cordial -- Copyright 2026 the Cordial
contributors, GNU General Public License v3.0, as their NOTICE states. That
text was imported with the maintainer line rewritten; the rest is only what
this repository's history shows to be its own work. The inherited text stays
GPL-3.0 as its authors licensed it, and nothing here speaks for them.

Where this file and upstream's own copy of the packaging have since
diverged -- upstream rewrote its pinning paragraph and added a line about
Roblox material -- the wording here is this repository's, and upstream's is
upstream's. Neither replaces the other.

Stating the boundary beats letting a reader infer it. The AUR submission
guidelines ask that a submission be licensed 0BSD and treat anything else as
a bar to promotion into the official repositories. On inherited text that
question can only be settled by whoever holds the copyright: a maintainer
cannot relicense another project's work by putting a license file beside it.
Upstream could settle it by licensing packaging/aur/ under 0BSD in its own
tree.
